fof_version: '0.1'
type: enemy
id: bought_sergeant
name: Sergeant-at-Arms
ruleset:
  modules:
  - id: base
    version: 0.1.0
enemy:
  tier: named
  attack_modifier: 2
  defense_modifier: 2
  armor: light
  techniques:
  - hold_the_terms
  special: HOLD THE TERMS — once per scene, the sergeant states the contract's boundary
    aloud. Every Blade in earshot immediately behaves as though the boundary is
    where the sergeant just said it is, whatever they believed a moment ago.
  description: The one reading the room instead of the target. Sergeants of the
    Bought carry the contract itself in a case at the hip, and produce it more readily
    than steel, because in their experience it settles more.
  disposition: Reads first, fights second, and would genuinely rather not.
  first_target: Whoever is closest to breaking the contract's boundary.
  triggers:
  - Opens by naming the contract's terms aloud. This is not a bluff; it is how the
    company works.
  - Spends Hold the Terms when the party splits, to keep the Blades from following
    anyone past the line.
  morale: Surrenders the field the moment the contract is void — payment withdrawn,
    terms broken by the employer, or the named target gone. Will say so out loud
    and expect to be believed.
  organization: One per four Blades.
  notes: 'TR breakdown: offense(+2 → 4) + durability(Resolve 3) + armor(light →
    1) + techniques(1) = 9.'
  negotiation: Wants the contract satisfied or voided; either ends the fight. Shifts
    for proof the employer has broken terms. Honours any deal that lets the company
    withdraw with its fee and its reputation.
  resolve: 3
created_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
last_modified: '2026-08-02T00:00:00+00:00'
